      "writtenOn": "2026-09-21T14:45:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The preferred way for Skia to do these stagings with Chrome would be for either:\n\na) Land a change to skia/config/SkUserConfig.h in chromium that defines `SK_LEGACY_GRAPHITE_READ_PIXELS_BOTTOM_LEFT_BEHAVIOR`, then guard the new code in Skia with a `!defined(SK_LEGACY_GRAPHITE_READ_PIXELS_BOTTOM_LEFT_BEHAVIOR)`. After rolling into chrome, you can then update SkUserConfig and cleanup the rest of chrome\u0027s bottom-left handling. Finally, then clean up the legacy code paths in Skia.\n\nb) Guard the new code in Skia with a `defined(SK_GRAPHITE_READ_PIXELS_SUPPORTS_BOTTOM_LEFT)` check. After rolling into chrome, you update skia/config/SkUserConfig.h to define `SK_GRAPHITE_READ_PIXELS_SUPPORTS_BOTTOM_LEFT` and fix its bottom-left handling. Lastly, you remove the legacy code path from Skia and then remove the now-unnecessary define from Chrome\u0027s SkUserConfig.h",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "0a9d78fb60d84566e84420942008743db6fd068d",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
