      "writtenOn": "2026-09-23T17:25:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, the easiest way to do that would be the first approach where the new flipping code is guarded by !defined(FLAG). You just have to land a change in Chrome that defines the FLAG first (one line CL to src/config/SkUserConfig.h).  Then when this main CL lands in Skia, Skia\u0027s waterfall will use the new behavior and Chrome will use the old behavior until we remove the define from SkuserConfig.h in chromium\u0027s repo.\n\nOtherwise, it is possible to configure certain builds on our tree to add extra defines but I don\u0027t think that\u0027s warranted here. We usually reserve that for an in-progress staging that will take quite a long time to migrate to the new behavior so we want to preserve testing both ways.",
      "parentUuid": "df55e485_1339a050",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "0a9d78fb60d84566e84420942008743db6fd068d",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
