      "writtenOn": "2026-09-21T14:45:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "WDYT about refacting the `asyncReadTexture()` function to take in the TextureFormatXferFn? Then we could use its `isIdentity()` function (or expose the additional nuanced `usesRP()` function) to decide whether or not to add an extra GPU conversion?  We\u0027d construct the XferFn in `asyncReadPixels` and then pass it down.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 797,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 803,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "0a9d78fb60d84566e84420942008743db6fd068d",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f9565f0d_b3b80628",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/Context.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 803,
      "author": {
        "id": 19434
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-22T16:56:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What could be a benefit of passing `TextureFormatXferFn` to `asyncReadTexture`?\nActually, I\u0027m curious can we make `transferPixels` decides to use CopyAsDraw or TextureFormatXferFn on its own?\n\nSome callers don\u0027t call `asyncReadTexture` and instead of call `transferPixels` directly. If we had to pass `TextureFormatXferFn` to `asyncReadTexture`, I feel we would have to repeat the TextureFormatXferFn construction in multiple call sites. Not to mention inside `asyncReadTexture` we would have to check again whether we want to do a GPU copy even though callers already checked that.",
      "parentUuid": "c47e9d5a_db8b7913",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 797,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 803,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "0a9d78fb60d84566e84420942008743db6fd068d",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "24d7fcc1_0081b43e",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/Context.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 803,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-22T18:12:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "TextureFormatXferFn is meant to be the logic that determines everything that has to happen in a data transfer (CPU-\u003eGPU or vice versa), in particular matching the differing semantics between SkColorType for CPU data and the texture format data on the GPU. If we can rely on it to decide whether or not to call into CopyAsDraw, we won\u0027t be surprised by missing a case of expensive CPU work.\n\nThe other calls to `transferPixels` are part of the YUV readback and they should always be the identity xfer function, so it could actually help things to explicitly pass that in there.\n\nThe other calls to `asyncReadTexture()` (outside of `asyncReadPixels()` that would decide to do the `CopyAsDraw()`) are limited to async-readback on an SkSurface that cannot be sampled. In that case, we can\u0027t use `CopyAsDraw()` so creating the default TextureFormatXferFn would be some duplicate code but it wouldn\u0027t be duplicate work.\n\nLastly, the codeflow inside `asyncReadPixels()` that calls back into itself after it\u0027s called `CopyAsDraw()` can likely be updated to just adjust the `view` and reset the xfer function (maybe assert that it should be the identity now?) and then proceed into `asyncReadTexture`.",
      "parentUuid": "f9565f0d_b3b80628",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 797,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 803,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "0a9d78fb60d84566e84420942008743db6fd068d",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
