      "lineNbr": 880,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-21T14:45:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ganesh\u0027s asyncReadback logic for bottom-left textures is to convert it to a temporary top-left texture by drawing it. I think we should do that here as well so that the only real logic for bottom-left in Graphite is applying the y flip matrix to its transform when we encounter it in a draw. Then it being bottom-left would just be part of the needsConversion check.\n\nI don\u0027t think we really need to worry about the case where Graphite is asked to readback from a texture that isn\u0027t sampleable AND bottom-left (since Graphite already requires that all renderable surfaces are top-left).\n\nBy including the y flip as a GPU conversion, we\u0027re more likely to hit the `xferFn-\u003eisIdentity()` path that allows us to provide the mapped GPU buffer directly to chrome.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 867,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 880,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "0a9d78fb60d84566e84420942008743db6fd068d",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b15ea723_24b62890",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/Context.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 880,
      "author": {
        "id": 19434
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-21T17:09:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I don\u0027t think we really need to worry about the case where Graphite is asked to readback from a texture that isn\u0027t sampleable AND bottom-left (since Graphite already requires that all renderable surfaces are top-left).\n\nNot sure I understood 100% but there are some formats that are not renderable but sampleable (i.e. R16G16Float). Sometime the image is imported from WebGL and it\u0027s bottom left. But it\u0027s not renderable in Graphite so we cannot convert/flip the pixels using a temporary R16G16Float texture IIUC. Hence I included both a GPU flip and a CPU flip as a fallback (if a GPU draw is not possible). I think it would be weird to allow some formats to flip and others just ignore the origin.",
      "parentUuid": "6e437c79_68e46cc4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 867,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 880,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "0a9d78fb60d84566e84420942008743db6fd068d",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d49e054c_819c24b7",
