      "lineNbr": 880,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-21T17:34:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A format not being renderable is a significant detail, but if a format is not renderable, then it cannot apply any of these conversions (alpha, colorspace, or flip) on the GPU. You\u0027re right that then we would need to have the CPU-side flip be possible as a fallback, so we should keep this code.\n\nHowever, I think we can still attempt to do the flip on the GPU just like we would with any other conversion.\n\n(not exactly related to this theory, but I think R16G16Float should be considered a renderable format looking at the flags that are reported for it in DawnGraphiteUtils capability table. Are you seeing it differently in practice?)",
      "parentUuid": "b15ea723_24b62890",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 867,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 880,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "0a9d78fb60d84566e84420942008743db6fd068d",
