      "writtenOn": "2026-09-23T17:25:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "kRGB_565 colortype should be considered renderable (so renderable_colortype takes the default branch and returns kRGB_565). However, if that\u0027s then failing, it means that the TextureFormat::kR5_G6_B5 or kB5_G6_R5 are not renderable on the hardware you\u0027re testing.  It is plausible for some hardware to let you create a 565 sampleable texture but not let you render to it (in that case Graphite\u0027s behavior is to fail, whereas Ganesh would start making guesses about switching to a different format with different components and precision potentially). \n\nIf you\u0027re testing a Dawn config, that\u0027s expected because Dawn/webgpu do not have 565 formats at all (but then I don\u0027t know how you\u0027d get the 565 source texture in the first place).",
